{"title":"2016 USAMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> be an acute triangle, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/f/49fa720465f48bcce1ae7b0ea340c6f2a865c05b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_B, I_C,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> denote its <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />-excenter, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />-excenter, and circumcenter, respectively. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are selected on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/c/a9c2f37be66c048fdff379cb3f9d5cb30ec40f48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABY = \\angle CBY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"138\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/a/ddab6040a219aa40b2edec485cdbe6b8bd90b38e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BE}\\perp\\overline{AC}.$\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> Similarly, points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> are selected on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/734cec74ebde6e3bceedbf29d3317298a2782a36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACZ = \\angle BCZ$\" width=\"134\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/927a04d7129dcb74b9de6fef1066f29abd90388d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CF}\\perp\\overline{AB}.$\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/5/4e5aafcca964c9311479c398f530a99053750108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_B F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f87932bab0a47b26e7dd6cb9782553afcbefc979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_C E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3ce33ec2a34dc4fddaec3224043f4a72bbe6d0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/2139700ff0992753a6a395d5d0a523125ece2945.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{PO}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/1/ad1817c383636a4e8f30eb3ebb5c8a26dd172742.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{YZ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> are perpendicular.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This problem can be proved in the following two steps.\n</p><p>1. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/2/822b800ca9993bd5686e4fe3a128c4659d3e979d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />-excenter, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/5/3a533881c47a195e35bfb8c1090638fa9add01b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_A,O,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are colinear. This can be proved by the Trigonometric Form of Ceva's Theorem for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/d/fad2db05e5fcd7d0c55666d5f1e70b55a5dacd25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle I_AI_BI_C.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>2. Show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/354d930afca316cdf5f7824c99d756c8f7a0c4b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_AY^2-I_AZ^2=OY^2-OZ^2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"225\" height=\"18\" /> which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd6d01b321f9e2dea430c54f0cf651f344c7a978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{OI_A}\\perp\\overline{YZ}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" /> This can be proved by multiple applications of the Pythagorean Thm.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2016_USAMO_3a.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/93/2016_USAMO_3a.png/300px-2016_USAMO_3a.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"232\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/93/2016_USAMO_3a.png/450px-2016_USAMO_3a.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/93/2016_USAMO_3a.png/600px-2016_USAMO_3a.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>We find point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/c/4fc53df7f73e8e399309780a18110428c4f38c6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YZ,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> we prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/f/0bf164ad93c61480ac39ab0360b60e01fd2fb8e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TY \\perp OI_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" /> and state that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/f/faf70d7970d734f0b9601da0c1a854bdf6fa6af7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X(24)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> from ENCYCLOPEDIA OF TRIANGLE, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/8/bf8f14a7cedc7a85eab11c4d5b715e9caf3a74ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P \\in OI_A.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" /> \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> be circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c79ddff6b45c6ad853d03d6231fdf0fba5ededb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O.$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> \nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaaa0bea097466e1752804c57debdf174f8cfb54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y_1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/c/28c367151db654c98df81eb7ab6e1d72b4233f10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> be crosspoints of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12f22a1b31a5520ddf8d999c899345f1f1ab70ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BY,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3aa046dd998cb08785d8be38c772e63b56ac28f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CZ,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> respectively.\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be crosspoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aab17e2f2005ca643854186430099294ad84b85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YZ$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c76729cb9153c8c11704f1d554a047e6bdf89bf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y_1 Z_1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />\nIn accordance the Pascal theorem for pentagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/e/07eeaf431695c6ad560ee97aa2df7afd9a1425d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AZ_1BCY_1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/5/8d5b93dbd5e47d3865c56f03ec1213bb82256a67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AT$\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/8207b79435a4bd499da7598fb44424c8a8499238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2016_USAMO_3b.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/20/2016_USAMO_3b.png/500px-2016_USAMO_3b.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"500\" height=\"268\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/20/2016_USAMO_3b.png/750px-2016_USAMO_3b.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/20/2016_USAMO_3b.png/1000px-2016_USAMO_3b.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/4/684152a4f5bbc9581ab9d7678a6da6d89a421b80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_A, I_B, I_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccf6d387ce491c0ca100c134021f21f616d75162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />-excenters of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919b9f77a6985e760286799909be5bfe0152f40e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />\nDenote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/8/908824a3fddada7b37c041be35cb4092f5f2c405.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = BC, b = AC, c = AB, 2\\alpha = \\angle CAB, 2\\beta = \\angle ABC, 2\\gamma = \\angle ACB,\\]\" width=\"524\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/5/7356368ac5fdb851fc298e2805856239b47778d3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\psi = 90^\\circ – \\gamma + \\beta, X = AI_A \\cap \\omega, X_1 = BC \\cap AI_A,\\]\" width=\"369\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/24959f08977e451147b2b509e57d6b7fad148773.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[I = BI_B  \\cap CI_C, U= YZ \\cap AI_A, W = Y_1Z_1 \\cap AI_A,\\]\" width=\"395\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the foot ot perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9eb08d7d4ce34ba6d2988a08b5348da6d10981c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI_A.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"36\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is ortocenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4eef313b5c6ea061a124562f374da70af9223b47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle I_A I_B I_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> and incenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919b9f77a6985e760286799909be5bfe0152f40e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> is the Nine–point circle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/c/23c4f15f2f51cfdc8414450dc6791551bfb29e68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle I_A I_B I_C.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/4050d664ce5c92ff00047194b106fe14626543e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/f/71fb9a86d04513e6ec7dd69734bf45df90d75584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II_B, Z_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/c/5cc6082cc2ec5b3512c53befb344858629d083d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"15\" /> in accordance with property of Nine–point circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/4/ef48ac956824fcaea163a530a717e6df694aa006.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"9\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/7/2b793c4c4fd94acc799b5f2c3a5506b5c9ea6e03.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Y_1Z_1 || I_B AI_C || VO, IW = AW \\implies TW \\perp AI.\\]\" width=\"367\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/a/43a9744837cffc745df4247aba70be7a88b51dac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle AXC = 180 ^\\circ – 2\\gamma – \\alpha = 90 ^\\circ – \\gamma + \\beta = \\psi.\\]\" width=\"309\" height=\"17\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/7/fa7fa3f9edfb840fc02fecd232ff2480909ed348.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle TAI = \\angle VOA = 2\\beta + \\alpha = 90 ^\\circ – \\gamma + \\beta = \\psi.\\]\" width=\"350\" height=\"17\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/1/701cf28064f25a66dcc9521da02a94f3bde79171.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[I_A X_1 = IX_1 = BX_1 = 2R \\sin \\alpha \\implies\\]\" width=\"284\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/4/c64648e70bd0190a5d567c6cfd082bd76003ae6f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cot \\angle OI_A A = \\frac {VI_A}{VO} = \\frac {R \\sin \\psi + 2R \\sin \\alpha}{R \\cos \\psi} = \\tan \\psi + \\frac{2 \\sin\\alpha}{\\cos \\psi}.\\]\" width=\"461\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a5379f1bc3b22e6518360795c6c5b9bab676118d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CX = \\frac {ab}{b+c} \\implies \\frac {AI}{IX}= \\frac {AC}{CX}= \\frac {b+c}{a} \\implies AI = AX \\frac {b+c}{a+b+c},\\]\" width=\"505\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/b/7eb113de8f17e40c4d1027de4dea3dfa1550e5fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AW = \\frac {AI}{2}, UW = AU – AW,\\]\" width=\"222\" height=\"37\" /> \nIn <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aab17e2f2005ca643854186430099294ad84b85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YZ$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> cross segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/1/8e146e0aa8d64162e19b35fc7719434ba807d9ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX \\implies \\frac {AU}{UX} = \\frac {m + nk}{k+1},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"209\" height=\"41\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f16efba4db8e4c57342695458fdfcb7b0daef8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\frac {a}{b}, m = \\frac{a}{c}, k=\\frac {b}{c},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"172\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/658b0a5f09db749e572864ade334c4f5cf34575f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {AU}{UX} = \\frac{2a}{b+c} \\implies  AU = AX \\cdot \\frac {b+c}{2a +b +c}.\\]\" width=\"330\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/f/d9ff05a2b3ac9f8f526dc15701a9c2511a60e1fb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {AU – AW}{AW} = \\frac {b+c} {2a + b + c}.\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"39\" />\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2016_USAMO_3c.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/bc/2016_USAMO_3c.png/400px-2016_USAMO_3c.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"363\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/bc/2016_USAMO_3c.png/600px-2016_USAMO_3c.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/bc/2016_USAMO_3c.png/800px-2016_USAMO_3c.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/2/c72f9db5c8bfc8ac56cabb80753e6128290696da.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cot \\angle UTW = \\frac {TW}{UW} = \\frac {AW \\cdot \\tan \\psi}{AU – AW} = \\tan \\psi \\cdot \\frac {2a +b+c}{b+c} =\\]\" width=\"446\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/ebaefe5a602e9c5dda05ab9d5cd4ea301fc93743.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\tan \\psi \\cdot \\frac {2a}{b+c} + \\tan \\psi = \\frac {2 \\sin \\alpha}{\\sin \\psi} \\tan \\psi + \\tan \\psi  = \\tan \\psi + \\frac{2 \\sin\\alpha}{\\cos \\psi}\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"40\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/d/1cdbe00714354b157c71fb57009c58f1059858a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies  \\angle UTW = \\angle OI_AA .\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/2/3d2d197006161495ef11b53bd373f621b1efb4fd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[TW \\perp AI_A \\implies TYZ \\perp OI_A.\\]\" width=\"241\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/0/27000bce3356e32e6f12284d8f3b3c031136c7b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle II_B I_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> be the base triangle with orthocenter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/27408a64abbc8de7da6ce5622ae63af4f97343be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_A,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> center of Nine-points circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/e/3ae5fb8674dbf1b5d31b67b2b2c48e0a8047137b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O \\implies OI_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" /> be the Euler line of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/c/31cabe62a8149f94ce2f258f49b017a5f366e35c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle II_B I_C.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is orthic triangle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/6/9d67eee20dc49e2913202af3cbd94c8a8aed6770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle II_B I_C,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872e3b09425c9659d782119a543dc858aa520a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is orthic-of-orthic triangle.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is perspector of base triangle and orthic-of-orthic triangle. \n</p><p>Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/f/faf70d7970d734f0b9601da0c1a854bdf6fa6af7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X(24)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> of ENCYCLOPEDIA OF TRIANGLE CENTERS which lies on Euler line of the base triangle.\n[<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/Kimberling%E2%80%99s_point_X(24)\">[1]</a>]\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2016_USAMO_3d.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/b8/2016_USAMO_3d.png/300px-2016_USAMO_3d.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"206\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/b8/2016_USAMO_3d.png/450px-2016_USAMO_3d.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/b8/2016_USAMO_3d.png/600px-2016_USAMO_3d.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><i><b>Claim</b></i>     <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/a/94acbb20c2f17069721c3c4f570884ec15831838.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {AU}{UX} = \\frac {m + nk}{k + 1}.\\]\" width=\"123\" height=\"39\" />         \n<i><b>Proof</b></i>  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53c8ecd25d261743a43c19b0c5751e16e543460.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {[AYZ]}{[ABC]} = \\frac {AZ \\cdot AY}{AB \\cdot AC} = \\frac {1}{(n + 1) \\cdot (m+1)},\\]\" width=\"315\" height=\"43\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/0/130b9fcb31dfc719b2a21dae6a4094ad697bea2f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {[BXZ]}{[ABC]} = \\frac {BZ \\cdot BX}{AB \\cdot BC} = \\frac {n}{(n + 1) \\cdot (k+1)},\\]\" width=\"315\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/a/6aa2e2e9645a2d24d72577706c7afa468de56caf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {[CXY]}{[ABC]} = \\frac {CY \\cdot CX}{AC \\cdot BC} = \\frac {mk}{(m + 1) \\cdot (k+1)},\\]\" width=\"321\" height=\"43\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/7/187e4126caf88629b032d58ea5edcf1f9baf1307.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {[XYZ]}{[ABC]} = 1 - \\frac {[AYZ]}{[ABC]} – \\frac {[BXZ]}{[ABC]} – \\frac {[CXY]}{[ABC]}  = \\frac {m+nk}{(m + 1) \\cdot (k+1)\\cdot (n+1)},\\]\" width=\"530\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/5/0351adc9ed8c24b21cbf516369c5b60967997c37.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {AU}{UX} = \\frac {[AYZ]}{[XYZ]} = \\frac {m + nk}{k + 1}.\\]\" width=\"207\" height=\"43\" /> \n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAMO\" title=\"2016 USAMO\">2016 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2016 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2016\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018002430\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.058 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.080 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 551/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1313/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18806/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclus